About the art

  The kaomoji and short text art in src/ascii/arts.js (for example Owata, Mona,
  Giko, Shobon, orz, the table flip, the shrug, the Lenny face and greentext)
  are traditional internet folk art. They were created and shared anonymously
  in communities such as 2channel, Reddit and 4chan over many years, and are
  widely believed to be free for anyone to use. This project does not claim
  ownership of them and credits them to those communities.

  The animation frames and timing written for this project are dedicated to
  the public domain to the extent possible (CC0 1.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).

Third-party code: none is bundled. The project has no runtime or build
dependencies. Wrangler (Cloudflare) is an optional external tool used during
development and is not distributed with this repository.

